@startuml imaging_service_request_workflow
title Imaging Service Request workflow (excluding MPPS)

autonumber

actor "EHR / EMR\n(Order Placer)" as ehr
participant "RIS\n(DSS / Order Filler)" as ris
participant "FHIR service\n(MWL data)" as fhir
participant "Modality\n(Acquisition Modality)" as modality
participant "Image archive /\nImage Manager" as archive

group RAD-2: create order
  ehr -> ris: Create imaging order
  ris -> fhir: $create-order\n(CreateOrderRequestBundle)
  note right of fhir
    ServiceRequest (ImagingServiceRequest)
    ServiceRequest (RequestedProcedure)
    Patient / Encounter
  end note
  fhir --> ris: OrderBundle\n(including Task / scheduled step)
end

group RAD-5: query modality worklist
  modality -> ris: DICOM C-FIND\n(MWL query parameters)
  ris -> fhir: Resolve MWL entry\nfrom Task and references
  note right of fhir
    Task (scheduled procedure step)
      -> RequestedProcedure
      -> ImagingServiceRequest
      -> Patient / Encounter
      -> Device (scheduled station)
      -> ImagingStudy (Study Instance UID)
  end note
  fhir --> ris: FHIR resource data
  ris --> modality: DICOM C-FIND-RSP\n(MWL entry)
end

group Acquisition and reconciliation
  modality -> archive: DICOM study\n(images)
  modality -> ris: Completion / status information\n(DICOM or local integration)
  ris -> fhir: Record performed work\n(optional Procedure) and update ImagingStudy
  fhir --> ris: Updated resource state
end

group RAD-3 / RAD-4 status communication
  ris --> ehr: Updated order status\n(RAD-3 / FHIR exchange)
  ris -> archive: Procedure/study reconciliation\n(RAD-4 / RAD-13)
end

note over modality,ris
  The IG defines the FHIR profiles and mappings for the order/MWL
  resource model. The completion transaction and the mechanism used
  to update the EHR are not specified as a single end-to-end workflow.
end note

@enduml
